  "body": "Found by the review of PR #837 (merged), reported by the maintainer.\n\n**What:** since #837 the simulation draws the tool from `sim_tool_body` and no longer goes through the tool-body view helpers:\n- `tool_body_view::assembly_for_operation` (`crates/app/src/tool_body_view.rs`, about line 245) has no callers anywhere in the tree.\n- `tool_body_view::bare_assembly` (about line 232) is used only by `crates/app/tests/tool_body_view.rs` (about lines 185 and 193).\n\n**Fix:** remove `assembly_for_operation`. For `bare_assembly`: remove it together with the test code that only exercises it, unless another caller exists by then (the tool editor's body column may still use the module's other functions - leave those alone). Whatever becomes unused as a result (imports, private helpers) goes too. No behaviour change.\n\nDone means: neither function has zero non-test callers (removed, or genuinely used), `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean, the remaining `tool_body_view` tests pass, and the `#[test]` count change is stated in the PR (only tests that existed solely for a removed function may go).\n",
